---
/**
 * Site-wide "under construction" strip, directly under the header.
 * Outline only, no fill — the schedule banner right below is the loud one,
 * and two solid strips stacked fought each other.
 *
 * **Keep the wording true.** It promised clips, videos and guides; two of the
 * three shipped on 2026-09-08, so by 2026-09-10 the strip was telling visitors
 * the site lacked things it had. Guides are the only thing genuinely still
 * missing, so that is all it now claims — and when they land, this component
 * should go rather than be reworded again.
 */
---
<div class="notice">
  <p class="container inner">
    <span class="tag">Ve výstavbě</span>
    <span>Web se pořád staví — návody teprve chystám.</span>
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .notice {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--card-edge);
  }
  /* Plain centred text rather than a flex row: a flex item cannot be narrower
     than its content, so on a narrow window (or at browser zoom) the sentence
     spilled past the page's content column and sat left of the header. */
  .inner {
    /* margin-block only — a plain `margin: 0` would wipe out the container's
       `margin-inline: auto`, leaving this 1200px box against the left edge
       with the text centred inside it rather than on the page. */
    margin-block: 0;
    padding-block: 0.6rem;
    text-align: center;
    text-wrap: balance;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .tag {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-right: 0.45rem;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.45rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
